# .env.example
# Changes:
# - Documented Firebase Web app ids so spaceswoosh.app events land in the
#   same Firebase project as iOS/Android (spaceswoosh-faa9c).
# - Documented vaisi's Project as the Away Open World leaderboard backend
#   (ref ptzaxgslzjefaxdkrvyr). Schema: supabase/migrations/*_high_scores_*.sql
#
# These values ship inside the client bundle by design — Supabase's anon key and
# RevenueCat's public SDK key are both meant to be public, and are safe only
# because the server enforces Row Level Security / receipt validation. Keeping
# them out of source control is hygiene (rotation, per-environment builds), not
# secrecy.
#
# CI must define the same variables:
#   - GitHub Actions (web deploy): repository secrets
#   - Codemagic (iOS/Android):     environment variable group "spaceswoosh"

# --- Supabase (Open World leaderboard) ---------------------------------------
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API (vaisi's Project for Away).
# If either is missing the game still runs; the leaderboard degrades to
# "unavailable" instead of crashing. Native iOS reads the same vars at
# xcodebuild time into Info.plist SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- RevenueCat (in-app purchases, native only) ------------------------------
# Project -> API keys. Platform-specific PUBLIC keys, not the secret key.
VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
VITE_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Firebase Analytics (web) -------------------------------------------------
# Project spaceswoosh-faa9c. Native iOS/Android use google-services files, not
# these. Register a Web app in Firebase Console → Project settings → Add app,
# then paste the Web appId here so Explorations shows platform=web. Measurement
# ID defaults to G-SMEY63Z40C if omitted. These are public client values.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-SMEY63Z40C
